  // TD-8 migration classifier — see docs/megiddo/test-database-tool/06-migration-classification.md
  //
  // GOLDEN HASH LOG — tests/fixtures/ork-db/golden-schema-catalogs.sha256 is one opaque
  // line, so a re-record is unreviewable unless what moved it is written down. Every
  // re-record gets a line here naming the tables the render's rows changed for.
  //
  //   2026-08-31 — RBAC coverage expansion. Rows only, no DDL: ork_permission (+22 keys,
  //   -2 keys), ork_role (+ork_admin) and ork_role_permission (crown / ork_admin /
  //   utility-role grants, minus the corrective delete of non-admin global-scope grants).
  //   No other table and no column moved; the rest of the render is byte-identical.
  //
  //   2026-08-31 (second re-record) — same migration, section 3b added: two UPDATE
  //   statements reconciling ork_permission.display_name/description for
  //   kingdom.park.create and kingdom.park.claim with PermissionRegistry, which
  //   INSERT IGNORE could not do for rows 2026-08-25-02 had already seeded. Rows in
  //   one table only; no DDL, no other table touched.
  //
  //   2026-09-01 — third re-record. Same migration again, post-review: the utility-role
  //   grants are now matched by role OWNERSHIP (kingdom_id) rather than by name across
  //   every kingdom, and global.admin.grant's advertised capability was corrected. Rows
  //   in ork_role_permission only; no DDL, no new file, no other table touched.
  //
  //   2026-09-01 — fourth re-record, after the post-review pass. Same migration; the
  //   utility-role grants and the global.admin.grant wording were revised again and the
  //   sandbox was rebuilt from scratch (an agent's over-broad cleanup had deleted two
  //   render-seeded kingdoms). Rows only; no DDL, no new file.
  //
  //   2026-08-31 (third re-record) — same migration, section 4's ork_admin exemption
  //   changed from `LOWER(r.name) <> 'ork_admin'` to `NOT (LOWER(r.name) = 'ork_admin'
  //   AND r.kingdom_id = 0)` so a kingdom-created role that merely borrows the name no
  //   longer keeps global-scope grants, plus comment-only edits. Affects which
  //   ork_role_permission rows the corrective DELETE removes; no DDL, no other table.
  //
